Validation and correctness
--------------------------
- Extend conversion and parser fixture coverage to the remaining optional
  package classes, RNA/custom alphabets, truncated input, and metadata that
  each external format promises to preserve. Native gap/CWM/higher-order
  round trips and representative TFBSTools conversions now have tests.
- Calibrate scanning/enrichment under matched IID and higher-order backgrounds;
  distinguish valid nulls from composition-mismatch stress tests. Keep the
  local benchmark harness/results out of commits unless explicitly requested.
- Assess background-weighted P-value-to-score inversion for the exhaustive
  method; its current sequence-count quantile is not a non-uniform-background
  inverse. Dynamic inversion is the documented preferred path for this case.
- Add adversarial shuffling tests for exact k-mer preservation, repeated or
  sparse sequences, disconnected unused vertices, and seeded reproducibility.
- Test negative-score comparison normalisation and KL-logo axis limits with
  explicit fixtures before deciding whether either needs a fix.
- Audit C++ error/interrupt handling at thread boundaries and allocation-heavy
  paths; preserve validation and exhaustive-enumeration safety limits.

Documentation
-------------
- Refresh published speed/hit-count examples after threshold fixes, using
  equivalent work and reproducible measurements rather than old timings.
- Add a compact non-standard-motif workflow for amino-acid/custom alphabets,
  higher-order motifs, and gaps using the original functions.
- Expand pseudocount, information-content filtering, and submotif examples as
  concrete user questions arise; avoid duplicating existing introductory text.
- Consider heatmap/track integration examples and a mutation-effect logo
  example; evaluate a separate documentation website only if size warrants it.

Feature work
--------------------
- Add explicit presence-only and/or best-hit-per-motif-per-sequence scanning;
  define strand handling and ties before implementing an allocation-saving path.
- Profile and implement chunked scanning with stable ordering and bounded
  memory; consider optional disk-backed output only after profiling.
- Add opt-in progress messages and safe cancellation to long-running functions.
- Add an enrichment HTML report with counts, controls, settings, and logos.
- Improve reader diagnostics for missing files and expose consistent, documented
  pseudocount controls where needed.
- Add an ambiguity-resolution helper with explicit sampling/replacement rules.
- Design alphabet remapping and methylated-DNA support together with background,
  higher-order, and reverse-complement rules; do not merely relabel rows.
- Investigate to_df()/update_motifs() warnings using a concrete failing example.

Methods projects
------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Differential positional enrichment between two sets of sequences.
- Spatial motif-cluster detection beyond pairwise sequence co-occurrence.
- Optional alignment scoring against background at overhangs, or distinct
  alignment-selection and reporting scores; first define statistical semantics.
- Extend calibrated comparison P-values beyond the DNA/RNA PCC lite workflow
  only where a supported use case justifies the added method.
